{
    "background_story": "Salvador grew up in a small town surrounded by the rolling hills of a steel-producing region. From a young age, he was fascinated by the fiery furnaces and the strong, resilient metal they produced. He began his apprenticeship at the local steel mill, learning the intricacies of the trade from his father, a veteran steelmaker. Salvador's dedication and natural talent quickly earned him a reputation as one of the most skilled steelmakers in the region. He took great pride in crafting high-quality steel for the community, from the beams that held up the town's buildings to the tools that farmers used in their fields. As the years passed, Salvador became a master steelmaker, known for his attention to detail and his ability to coax even the most stubborn metals into submission. His work was not just a job, but a way to contribute to the community and leave a lasting legacy.",
